==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{L.}} word ''[[insignia#Latin|insignia]]'', plural of the word ''[[insigne#Latin|insigne]]'' meaning "[[emblem]]" and "[[symbol]]".

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# a [[patch]] or other object that [[show]]s what official or military [[rank]] someone has, or which [[group]], or organization they belong to.
# a [[symbol]] or token of personal [[power]], status or office, or of an official body of government or jurisdiction.

